      "body": "## Summary\n\nWeight update endpoints modify persistent model state and should not be accessible with an ordinary API key alone. Following the pattern from #44242, add the `admin_api_key` check to 9 weight-related endpoints:\n\n- `/update_weights_from_disk`\n- `/update_weights_from_tensor`\n- `/update_weights_from_distributed`\n- `/update_weights_from_ipc`\n- `/update_weight_version`\n- `/init_weights_update_group`\n- `/destroy_weights_update_group`\n- `/begin_weight_update`\n- `/end_weight_update`\n\nWhen the server is started without `--admin-api-key`, these endpoints now return 400 instead of allowing access with just `--api-key`.\n\nNote: This PR is based on main and may need a rebase after #44242 merges (both touch `test_http_server_auth_levels.py`).\n\nSigned-off-by: bantianyue <bantianyue@gmail.com>\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38552942540](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38552942540)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38552942530](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38552942530)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38552942488](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38552942488)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
